"hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1276,"Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami told us, Abdullah bin Daoud told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “only prayed the two rak’ahs after the afternoon prayer, because he had not yet prayed ""Noon is something"""
1277,"Al-Sana’ani Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Umm Salamah said: He entered upon me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after the afternoon prayer, and he prayed two rak’ahs. I said: O Messenger of God, what prayer is this? What were you praying? He said: “A delegation from Bani Tamim came and they distracted me from two rak’ahs that I used to perform in the afternoon.” I have mentioned the details of this news in the book Al-Kabir. Abu Bakr said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed two rak’ahs voluntarily after the afternoon prayer, fulfilling the two rak’ahs that he had prayed after Dhuhr, if his prohibition against praying after the afternoon prayer until the sun had set had been the fulfillment of all voluntary prayers, it would not have been permissible for him to make up the two rak’ahs that he had been praying. After noon, he makes them up after the afternoon prayer, but he only prays them out of his desire to continue doing voluntary work. Because he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told us that the best deeds are those that are constant, and whenever he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did a job, he liked to do it constantly."
1278,"The evidence for what I mentioned is that Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail bin Ja`far told us, Muhammad, who is Ibn Abi Harmala, told us, On the authority of Abu Salama, that he asked Aisha about the two prostrations that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform after the afternoon prayer in her house. She said: He used to pray them before the afternoon prayer, then he was distracted or forgot them, so he prayed them after the afternoon prayer, then he fixed them, and when He prayed a prayer that proved it.”"
1279,"And in the report of Jabir bin Yazid bin Al-Aswad Al-Sawa’i, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to the two men after he finished praying: Fajr: “If you prayed on your journeys, then you come and the imam is praying, then pray with him, and it will be a voluntary prayer for you.” I will take it out, God willing. Completely. Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Ziyad bin Ayyub narrated it, saying: Hushaym told us, Ya’la bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid. Al-Sawa’i, on the authority of his father, Abu Bakr said: And the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in this report, commanded whoever prayed Fajr on his journey to pray with Imam, and know that his prayer with the imam is voluntary. If the prohibition of praying after dawn until the sun rises was a general prohibition and not a specific prohibition, it would not It is permissible for someone who prays Fajr while traveling to pray with the imam and make it voluntary, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reported: “There will be rulers over you. They delay the prayer beyond its time, so pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them a rosary.” This indicates that if the Imam delays the afternoon prayer, Or Fajr, or both, a person must pray both prayers at their appointed time, then pray with the imam and make his prayer with him a rosary, and this A voluntary prayer after dawn and after the afternoon prayer, and I had dictated before the news of Qais bin Qahd, who was of this type, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He had enjoined the Banu Abd Manaf and the Banu Abd al-Muttalib from preventing anyone from praying at home at any hour of the day or night he wanted."
1280,"Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala and Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim, H. Muhammad bin Yahya and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, H. Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam told us, Muhammad bin Bakr told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Abu Al-Zubayr told me that he heard Abdullah Ibn Babah narrates, on the authority of Jubayr Ibn Mutim, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, this news of Ataa: “O Banu Abd Manaf, O Banu Abd “Al-Muttalib, if there is anything to you about the matter, I do not know why you have prevented anyone from praying at this house at any hour of the day or night he wanted.” This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, except that Ahmad ibn Al-Miqdam said: If you have any issue with the matter, and he said: Any hour of the day or night."
